  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000 (later adjusted to $550,000 to include real-time analytics). The project has progressed through several phases: the design phase was completed, followed by the development phase led by Omar Jensen. A strategic partnership with TechInnovate was established to aid AI research goals. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session on September 10th. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the achievement of the first major milestone ahead of schedule, involving a successfully tested prototype for secure file sharing. The next phase involves user interface enhancements planned for October, followed by a celebration on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective from January next year."
